Laser Line Scan - an open laser-perception kit
This product includes software developed at Nidvue (https://nidvue.com).

The following files are licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 or (at your option) any later version (GPL-3.0-or-later); see
LICENSE in this directory. They cover the complete laser-perception pipeline:
spectral illumination design, camera/laser calibration, sub-pixel stripe
extraction, search-band extraction, scatter recovery and dense 3D
reconstruction.

  board-pose.js         camera intrinsics/distortion and board pose
  charuco-board.js      ChArUco target geometry
  charuco-worker.js     ChArUco corner detection and calibration
  encoder-model.js      affine command-to-plane (galvanometer) mapping
  stripe-roi.js         calibration-derived geometric search region
  scatter.js            scatter-tail and saturated-shoulder recovery
  rows-pca.js/.json/.f32 trained row-level laser gate
  spectral.js           spectral design model (lamp/laser/filter/sensor)
  spectral-gl.js        WebGPU/WebGL preview of the spectral design
  spectral-plot.js      spectrum plotting widget
  viewer.js             3D point-cloud viewer
  rig-scene.js          rig schematic
  image-preview.js      frame preview widget
  calibration-report.js Markdown / PowerPoint calibration report
  locale.js             number and date formatting
  lab.css               laboratory styles
  core.wasm / oss.ts    kernel: Steger/Hessian extraction, plane fits

